## Key Sourcing Notes & Cross-Verification

### 1. GWP Basis Confirmation
<div style="border-left:4px solid #22C55E;background:#F0FDF4;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">The H1'FY25 deck's FY2024 comparative GWP of ₹5,607.6 Cr ties out exactly to the statutory "Gross Premium Written" of ₹5,60,727 Lakhs (₹5,607.27 Cr) shown in the September 30, 2024 IRDAI disclosure <doc_source>step9web1</doc_source>, confirming the deck's GWP series is on the <strong>statutory (with 1/n)</strong> basis — consistent with the task's preferred methodology. Total GWP (₹3,241.5 Cr) and Retail Health GWP (₹2,201.3 Cr) for H1FY25 are reported with confidence on this basis <doc_source>step12web1</doc_source>.</div>

### 2. NWP / NEP / Net Worth Reconciliation
NWP (₹2,544.9 Cr) and NEP (₹2,231.2 Cr) as shown in the H1'FY25 investor deck's KPI table reconcile with the statutory Revenue Account line items ("Net Premium Written" and "Premium Earned (Net)") in the September 30, 2024 filing once the OCR-scrambled lakh figures are correctly rebased <doc_source>step9web1</doc_source>. Net Worth of ₹2,064.6 Cr matches the statutory Balance Sheet figure of ₹2,06,455 Lakhs exactly at September 30, 2024 <doc_source>step9web1</doc_source>.

### 3. Claims Ratio (IFRS) & Commission Ratio — Not Disclosed
Neither the H1'FY25 investor presentation nor the statutory quarterly disclosure separately publishes an IFRS-basis claims ratio or a standalone commission ratio for H1FY25 — only the aggregate IGAAP Expense ratio is shown (Claims Ratio **62.5%** + Expense Ratio **41.0%** = Combined Ratio **103.5%**) <doc_source>step12web1</doc_source>.

### 4. PAT: IGAAP vs. IFRS Divergence
<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">The deck's explicit "I-GAAP to IFRS Reconciliation" table shows a <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">▼ marginal net loss of ₹(5.8) Cr under IGAAP</span> versus a <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">▲ positive PAT of ₹59.5 Cr under IFRS</span> for H1'FY2025 — the swing is driven mainly by the IFRS-17 insurance contracts adjustment of <strong>+₹96.5 Cr</strong> <doc_source>step12web1</doc_source>.</div>

### 5. Regulatory Overhang — EoM Forbearance Application
<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;"><strong>Material risk flagged in statutory filing:</strong> The September 30, 2024 statutory results disclose (Note 6) an <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">unresolved application for forbearance on Expense of Management (EOM) breach</span> for FY23 and FY24, with IRDAI issuing a show-cause notice on October 18, 2024. ₹162.05 Cr of excess EOM was transferred from the Revenue Account to the P&L Account for H1FY25 <doc_source>step9web1</doc_source> — this is a risk factor not reflected in the headline investor-deck EoM ratio of 40.0% reported above, and should be weighed when interpreting expense efficiency trends.</div>

### 6. Filing Date Basis
Both the statutory results and the H1'FY25 investor presentation were approved/released in conjunction with the Board meeting dated <strong>November 25, 2024</strong> <doc_source>step9web1</doc_source>; the presentation carries no separate letterhead date, so this Board meeting date is used as the best available filing-date proxy across all rows in the table above.</ans>
