icket size per policy | \u20b9 | 26,084 | 28,797 | 28,965 | 30,839 |\n| GWP per policy sold by Agents | \u20b9 | 22,895 | 25,028 | 24,160 | 25,108 |\n\n---\n\n1 Building a Granular, Growth Oriented and Profitable Health Insurance Franchise\n\nRetail Health GWP & Market Share\n\nRetail Health Market Share\n\n---\n\nComprehensive Portfolio of Innovative Health Insurance Products Across All Stages \n2\nof the Customer Lifecyle\n\nWELLNESS FOCUSED\n\n[Image: Image337]\n[Image: Image335]\n\n[Image: Image339]\n\nDISEASE\nMANAGEMENT\n\n[Image: Image341]\n\nHEALTH PLUS\n\n[Image: Image362]\n\n[Image: Image341]\n\nEMBEDDED\n\nMILLENNIALS\n\nHEALTH PLUS\n\n[Image: Image349]\n\nADVISORY\n\nSENIOR CITIZEN\n\nProduct with \u201cIndustry-First\u201d Features\n\nAFFLUENT\n\nMASS AFFLUENT\n\n[Image: Image335] [Image: Image360]\n\nHNI\n[Image: Image350]\n\n---\n\nEnabling Access to a 360\u00b0 Health and Wellness Ecosystem Platform, Providing a \n2\nHolistic Customer Health Proposition\n\nHEALTH OFFERINGS\n\nHome delivery of medicines\n\nBooking individual diagnostic \ntests with home sample \ncollection\n\nDigital consultations and \nsecond medical opinion\n\nAccess health education \ncontent on diseases published \nby Bupa and wellness content\n\nWELLNESS OFFERINGS\n\nCurated products offering \ndiscounts if a minimum step \ncount is achieved to \nencourage healthy living\n\nHealth assessment tools such as \nBMI and stress calculator\n\nHealthcare provider quality \nand infrastructure matrix\n\n---\n\nWe Measure NPS Across 35 Touch Points and are Focused on Continuously \n2\nImproving Customer Experience\n\n1\nWeighted Episodal NPS\n\n\u2022 21 Lakh+ customers were reached out seeking feedback in H1\u2019FY2025\n\n\u2022 2 Lakh+ customer responses received in H1\u2019FY2025\n\nNote:\n1. NPS score of few critical touch points (claims discharge, service, policy issuance, renewal etc.) is combined into a single, weighted NPS score, calculated as weighted average\n\n---\n\n3 Multi-Channel & Diversified Distribution with Emphasis on Digital Sales\n\nDiversified Channel Mix with Strong Focus on Growing High Value Channels\nH1\u2019FY2025 (%)\n\nIndividual Agents\n\nCorporate Agent -\nBanks\n\nNotes:\n1. Brokers include PB Fintech (Policybazaar)\n2. Others include Web Aggregators,, Insurance Marketing Firms, Point of Sales and Common Service Centers\n\nBanks and Other Corporate Agents\n\n[Image: Image487]\n\n163,483 Individual \nAgents\n[Image: Image456]\n[Image: Image452]\n\n508 Brokers\n[Image: Image460]\n[Image: Image452]\n\nInsurance Brokers\n\n[Image: Image479]\n[Image: Image481]\n\n[Image: Image477]\n\n---\n\n4 Our Technology Enables us to Serve Customers Anywhere, Anytime\n\nDigital Self-Serve Capabilities\n[Image: Image491]\n\nInsta Assist and \nCia Chatbot\n[Image: Image518]\n[Image: Image491]\n\nClaim Submission\n[Image: Image515]\n[Image: Image491]\n\n[Image: Image517]\n[Image: Image397]\n[Image: Image491]\n\nOne-Click \nRenewal\n[Image: Image518]\n[Image: Image491]\n\n99.9% new policies applied \nvia website and mobile apps\n[Image: Image495]\n[Image: Image493]\n\n---\n\nOur Value Chain is Significantly Automated with Analytics Embedded into \n4\nOperations\n\nPartner Onboarding\n\nModular API based\npartner integration\n\nDigital Dukaan and Niva Bupa \nUNO mobile applications for \nagent training\n\nCustomer Sourcing\n\n99.9%\n\nNew policies applied \ndigitally\n\nReal-time lead scoring \nsupported by product \nrecommendation engine\n\nUnderwriting\n\nPayments made digitally\n\nRule based automated \ndecisioning\n\nRetail policies autodecisioned\n\nLTV-based approach to \nidentify upsell or cross-sell \nopportunities\n\n90.1%\n\nDigital claims submission\n\nPolicy renewal without \nhuman intervention\n\nPredictive machine-based \nlearning model to target \nhigh lapse probability cases\n\nOutlier detection tool used \nfor billing review\n\n---\n\n5 Disciplined Underwriting and Business Selection Through LTV-Based Approach\n\nCOST OF \nACQUISITION\n\nRISK PERCEPTION\n\nREQUIRED\nRETURN ON \nCAPITAL\n\nFollow-Up \nAction\n\nProduct-to-customer, segmentto-channel mapping\n[Image: Image631]\n\nOver Index\n\nVery High\n\nPromote\n\nHigh\n\n[Image: Image647]\n[Image: Image631]\n\nIdentify opportunities for upsell \nor cross-sell to customers with \nhigh LTV\n[Image: Image631]\n\nAcceptable\n\nNegative\n\nDecision \nVectors\n\nAvoid\n\nCustomized and pre-qualified \noffers for each customer\n[Image: Image631]\n\nSales channel alignment of \nincentives and monthly review \nto increase renewals\n[Image: Image631]\n\n---\n\n## 5 Our Multi-Pronged Claims Management Strategy\n\n### Developing Partnerships and Strengthening Relationships with Network Hospitals\n\n# 1Expansion of Network of Preferred Partner Network (PPN) Hospitals\n\n### Auto Adjudication\n\n# 2Paperless Auto Adjudication Portal for Health Insurance Claims Processing\n\n### Robust Fraud Detection\n\n**3**Real Time Detection of Outliers in Claims Based on Disease, Treatment Provider, Location And Policy Seller **Billing Review**\n\n# 4Random Checks and Case-Specific Triggers to Identify Anomalies\n\n### Case Management\n\nCost Component Review on a Claim-by-Claim Basis with Medical Providers\n\n---\n\nOur Growing Hospital Network and PPN Hospitals Helps Improve Customer \n5\nSatisfaction Levels While Improving Control on Cost of Claims\n\nRapidly Growing Network of Hospitals (#)\n\nRapidly Growing Preferred Partner Network (#)\n\nFree ambulance \nservices and \ndesignated \nrelationship manager\n\nDiscount on \npharmacy, diagnostics \nand consultations \neven after discharge\n\nPreferred Partner Network Live in Cities (#)\n\nBenefits of PPN Hospitals\n\nFor Niva Bupa\n\n---\n\n5 Our Domain Knowledge and Experience in Claims Cost Management\n\nEnd-to-End Cashless Claims Auto Adjudication\n\nRetail Health Claims Cost Index1 I CAGR2- 6.6%\n\nReduction in processing time for pre-authorization of\ncashless claims through manual processing vs auto-adjudication \nclaims system\n[Image: Image746]\n[Image: Image742] [Image: Image744]\n\nThe change in index is on account of medical cost \ninflation, change in disease mix, medical 4\nadvancement etc. \n[Image: Image748]\n\n---\n\n6 Focus on Talent Management & Execution\n\nnd\nRanked 62 among Top 100 India's \nBest Companies To Work For 2024\n\nFeatured amongst India's Best Workplaces \nfor Millennials 2024: Top 50 (Large)\n\n---\n\n# Agenda\n\n## Our Strategy\n\n## Financial Performance\n\n---\n\nFinancial Performance\n\nGross Written Premium (GWP)\n\n(\u20b9 in Crores)\n\nProfit/(Loss) After Tax (I-GAAP)\n\n(\u20b9 in Crores)\n\nCombined Ratio\n\nProfit/(Loss) After Tax (IFRS)\n\n---\n\nReconciliation from I-GAAP to IFRS\n\n| Particulars(\u20b9in Crores) | FY2023 | FY2024 | H1&#x27;FY2024 | H1&#x27;FY2025 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Profit After Taxes as per I-GAAP | 12.5 | 81.9 | (79.8) | (5.8) |\n| IFRS Adjustments |  |  |  |  |\n| Insurance Contracts[IFRS-17] | 13.8 | 68.7 | 121.3 | 96.5 |\n| Leases[IFRS-16] | (3.2) | (3.0) | (1.5) | (0.7) |\n| Financial Instruments[IFRS-09] | (1.7) | 3.5 | 0.6 | (0.7) |\n| Share-based Payment[IFRS-02] | (9.4) | (8.8) | (4.3) | (7.2) |\n| Employee Benefits[IAS-19] | - | 0.7 | 0.7 | 0.9 |\n| Income Taxes[IAS-12] | (3.5) | (36.6) | (9.4) | (23.4) |\n| Profit After Taxes as per IFRS | 8.5 | 106.4 | 27.6 | 59.5 |\n\n---\n\nRobust Approach to Investment Management has Resulted in Strong Growth in \nAUM and Yield\n\nAUM Growth\n(\u20b9 in Crores)\n\nBreakup by Ratings\n% of Book Value of Debt Securities| H1\u2019FY2025\n\nNote:\n1. Investment Yield is on Annualized basis for H1\u2019FY2025\n\n---\n\n# Appendix\n\n---\n\nShareholding Pattern (as on November 13, 2024)\n\nTotal Shares Outstanding 1,827,026,398\n\nTop Institutional Shareholders\n\n| Investor Name | % Holding^ |\n| --- | --- |\n| Temasek | 4.51% |\n| Motilal Oswal Private Equity | 2.65% |\n| A91 Partners | 2.14% |\n| Amansa Capital | 1.96% |\n| FSSA Investment M